## N — Norms

- Data-only change; no schema/entity/enum changes; no Java code changes anywhere in this repo.
- Upsert-idempotent, matching `ddl-auto=update`'s persistent-schema convention.
- Category *names* are immutable from this spec's perspective.
- Existing 8 assets' values (beyond the 6 `NULL` capacity backfills) and the original 20 bookings' amounts/dates/customer are not touched, except the two documented `status` corrections.
- Every spec-band in every category has at least 1 asset — no category has a band left at 0.
- Payment/DeliveryRecord/ReturnRecord completeness is a status-driven rule applied uniformly across the **entire** booking set, scaled to whatever the final booking count is — not a fixed row count carried over from an earlier draft.

## S — Safeguards

- Do not rename or restructure `asset_categories.name`.
- Do not introduce a second seeding mechanism alongside the existing `data.sql`/upsert convention — extend it. No `CommandLineRunner`/`@PostConstruct` seeder for booking dates.
- Do not change bookings' `ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING` to `DO UPDATE` in this branch.
- Do not leave any booking — old or new — without a `BookingItem`, or without the `Payment`/`DeliveryRecord`/`ReturnRecord` rows its status implies.
- Do not leave any category spec-band at 0 assets, and do not put more than 1 asset in a band other than the deliberate 4-asset one (that recreates either the empty-band-fallback risk or an unintentional second point of depth that wasn't sized/verified).
- Do not fabricate rate ranges outside each category's existing `min_daily_rate`/`max_daily_rate` spread.
- Do not touch any existing asset's capacity/height/condition/rate fields (other than the 6 `NULL` capacity backfills) or any existing booking's amount/date/customer fields (other than the two named `status` corrections), and do not add new photo files.
- Do not size the Payment/DeliveryRecord/ReturnRecord backfill against a smaller booking-count estimate than what actually gets seeded — it must cover all ~74–101 bookings, not just the 10 backfilled orphans or a partial slice of the new ones.
- Do not change `SPEC-seed-data.md` or `data.sql` as part of authoring this plan — those are updated when the plan is actually executed, not now.

## Key decisions

| Decision | Why |
|---|---|
| One 4-asset band + exactly 1 asset in every other band, per category (27 total), not "3-in-band + 1 singleton" (16 total) | A singleton band can only ever report `0`/`1` `period_utilization`, forever — no different in kind from the original 2-asset-per-category bug, just relocated to a second band. Since every value here is freely chosen fixture data, there's no reason to introduce that on purpose. An empty band is also avoided, since its fallback behavior lives in Haystack code this repo can't inspect |
| 27, not 24 (the original v1 draft's number) | Coincidence of arriving near the same fleet size through a different, better-justified path: not "headroom," but "one band with real depth, every other band with real (if binary) coverage, zero empty bands, zero singleton-shaped depth-bands" |
| Zero existing asset values changed | Every existing asset already lands naturally into either its category's chosen 4-asset band or an already-correct filler position once the band choice accounts for what's already set (scissor lift, boom lift, fork lift) or still free (`NULL` excavator capacities) |
| Reuse existing images by brand, no new photos | New assets are new models under an already-seeded brand+category; duplicating that brand's existing base64 avoids new source files at a bounded (~3.4x) size cost |
| New booking dates stay `CURRENT_DATE`-relative via `data.sql`, no new seeding mechanism | Matches the existing convention exactly; `data.sql` already does this successfully for all 20 existing bookings |
| Don't attempt to fix the underlying staleness-on-freeze behavior | Requires changing bookings to `DO UPDATE` semantics — larger, riskier, not justified by any acceptance scenario |
| Booking ids 2 and 6 relabeled, not deleted/re-inserted | Every other row already associated with each already matches the corrected status exactly |
| Payment/DeliveryRecord/ReturnRecord completeness explicitly scaled with booking count | Booking volume grew across three revisions of this plan (20 → ~50-60 → ~74-101); the status-driven table's *shape* doesn't change, but its row *count* must track whatever the final booking total actually is, or this spec recreates its own "orphaned data" problem one table over |
| Category names untouched | Mismatch is a Haystack read-time concern, not a data defect |
| Extend existing `data.sql`/upsert mechanism, don't replace it | `ddl-auto=update` means schema and data persist between runs; a second seeding path risks conflicting with the upsert convention already in place |
